From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FramePlayer contributors <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 14:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 9/13] xr: Linux OpenXR draws pages at their own framebuffer
 size

A page that asks for XRWebGLLayer framebufferScaleFactor other than the
default (Down asks for 0.82) stayed black on Linux: Blink attaches the
shared image to a framebuffer whose depth buffer has the page's
framebuffer size, but the Vulkan binding always made its shared images
the swapchain's size, so the framebuffer was incomplete ("Attachments
are not all the same size") and every draw failed.

- The intermediate images, and the SharedImages made from them, have the
  page's framebuffer size (the layer's transfer size, which
  UpdateLayerBounds sets), and ResizeSharedBuffer replaces only the slot
  it is given instead of all of them.
- OnSwapchainImageReady resizes the slot the page draws into next, as
  the Android binding does, so slots follow a new size as they come up.
- RenderLayer scales an image of another size to fill the swapchain image
  with vkCmdBlitImage (linear filter), as Android draws a full-viewport
  quad; same-size images are still copied with vkCmdCopyImage.
  gpu::VulkanFunctionPointers has no vkCmdBlitImage, so the context
  resolves it with vkGetDeviceProcAddr.

Touches only device/vr/openxr/linux, which no other patch changes.
